# env files
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.env
*.env.*
# ...but the committed templates must survive the patterns above. Without these
# negations `*.env.*` swallows `.env.example`, and the one variable the build
# depends on ends up documented nowhere.
!.env.example
!*.env.example

